 "about_text": "Satoko Oe Contemporary (S.O.C.) is a contemporary art gallery in the Shirakawa district of Koto, Tokyo, which opened on 13 February 2016. The gallery represents a small roster of Japanese and international artists working across painting, sculpture, video and installation, including Takuya Ikezaki, Mitsuhiro Ikeda, Tadasuke Iwanaga, Teppei Kaneuji, Shinichiro Kano, Makiko Masutani, Chihiro Mori and Kesang Lamdark. Its exhibition program has also featured painters such as Shigeru Hasegawa and social-practice artist Yoshinori Niwa. The gallery has participated in art fairs abroad and joined with three other Tokyo galleries (Hagiwara Projects, Koki Arts and Maki Fine Arts) under the collective name Hammock for joint fair presentations.",
